course: dictionary
lesson: 9820
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which one is right. «A curling stone slides far because smooth ice has very little friction, and the sweepers smooth and warm the ice to make it glide further.» Here the clues are curling, ice and stone, so the sweepers are players brushing the ice, not cleaners.
explain: Look for clues. If the sentence is about a street, a road or a carpet, a sweeper is a person or machine that cleans. If it is about football, a sweeper is a defender who stays behind the other players to stop attacks.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in the meaning. Does "a defender who plays behind the other defenders" make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A sweeper is a person whose job is to sweep, such as a «street sweeper» or «road sweeper».
fact: A sweeper can also be a machine or tool for sweeping, such as a «carpet sweeper».
fact: In football, a sweeper is a defender who plays behind the other defenders to stop attacks.
fact: In curling, a sweeper brushes the ice in front of the stone to help it slide further.
fact: Sweeper is a noun: one sweeper, two sweepers.
exercise: «The sweepers smooth and warm the ice to make it glide further.» What are the sweepers doing in this curling sentence? | Hanging washing out to dry | Driving a big road-cleaning truck | *Brushing the ice in front of the stone | Playing as a defender in football
exercise: In football, what is a sweeper? | A street worker who cleans the pavements | A tool for cutting grass | *A defender who plays behind the other defenders to stop attacks | A machine for cleaning carpets
exercise: Which phrase names a tool for cleaning a floor? | street party | curling stone | *carpet sweeper | football pitch
test: A road sweeper came down our street early this morning. What is a road sweeper? | A player who stops attacks in football | A kind of bird that sings at dawn | *A person or truck whose job is to sweep the roads | A stone that slides across the ice
test: In curling, what do the sweepers brush? | The football pitch | Their own shoes | A carpet in the hall | *The ice in front of the stone
exam: The word sweeper has several meanings, so how do you choose the right one? | *Use the context, the words and sentences around it | Guess the first meaning you remember | Pick the longest meaning | Skip the word and never come back to it
